    name: 'CritterFest',
    title: 'CritterFest',
    description:
      'Lubbock’s largest annual animal event, CritterFest 2025, returns Thursday through Sunday, June 19-22, from 10:00 a.m. to 6:00 p.m. daily at the Science Spectrum. This exciting four-day event transforms the museum into a lively zoo featuring elephants, alligators, camels, reptiles, and many more fascinating animals. Enjoy thrilling animal acts, a popular petting zoo, pony and camel rides, and live reptile shows. Two headline shows, Avian Aces: Birds of Flight and Crocodile Encounters, highlight the event with educational and entertaining experiences showcasing powerful birds and remarkable reptiles. Showtimes vary daily, with multiple performances throughout the day. Your ticket grants access to all animals, shows, and regular museum exhibits, including Texas Alive: the Brazos River Journey!, a large aquarium exhibit. Tickets are sold at the door only: Adults $15, children (3-12) and seniors $12.50, with discounted rates for museum members. Children under 2 enter free. Additional fees may apply for animal feedings, rides, or photos. For more information, call 806-745-2525 or visit sciencespectrum.org.',
